# Image request: 0001 node GUI widget kit

- **From:** Claude Code
- **Created:** 2026-11-14 20:42 -05:00
- **Purpose:** Show each node GUI widget in the Patina theme, so that node GUIs look like the
  rest of the editor.
- **Output:** `docs/mockups/0001-node-gui-widget-kit-v1.png`
- **Size:** 3200 x 2000 if the tool can make it. Else the largest landscape size that it can
  make. Do not upscale a smaller image. Report the real size.
- **Background:** opaque, the panel color of the editor, #202020.
- **References:** `docs/gui-visual-guide.md`: use its palette, sizes and widget rules.
  `docs/mockups/mockup-9-smart-material-editor.png`: the main theme reference. Keep its fonts,
  corner radius and density, with the neutral surfaces of the guide instead of its blue cast.
- **Spec:** 4.3 (Node GUI), 15.3 (Visual rules). Common rules and icons:
  `docs/mockup-plan.md`.
- **Previous request:** none

## Brief

A design sheet, not an app window. Three labeled columns for the widget groups of spec 4.3.
The Canvas column also holds the custom widgets and the viewport. Each widget has a small
caption under it.

**Basic** column:

- Label.
- Button in four states: normal, hover, pressed, disabled.
- Toggle, off and on.
- Slider, with its value at the right end.
- Number field, with a drag cursor hint.
- Text field: empty with a placeholder, filled, focused.
- Dropdown: closed, and open with three options.

**Values** column:

- Color picker: a swatch, a saturation-value square, a hue strip and a hex field.
- Curve: a small tone curve with four points.
- Plot: a line plot with axes and two series.
- Table: three columns, four rows and a header row.
- Image: a thumbnail with its size label.
- Waveform: an audio waveform with a playhead.

**Canvas** column: one canvas that shows its primitives: lines, rectangles, circles, text and an
image. Under it, four custom controls that node authors build on a canvas: a gradient editor
with color stops, a 2D transform gizmo over an image, an envelope editor with four handles, and
a timeline with keyframes. Under them, a **Viewport**: a dark GPU surface with a lit 3D cube and
a small axis gizmo in one corner, with the caption "Large and full size only".

Bottom strip, two rows:

1. **Compact and large:** the same slider, dropdown and curve at the compact size of a node body
   and at the large size of the inspector. The compact size is smaller and denser, but stays
   readable.
2. **Fill color comparison:** a slider, a toggle and a button in the default neutral style
   (light gray fill), next to the same three filled with the example header color, the
   processing teal #175C59 of the guide.

Style:

- Neutral fills by default. The widgets belong to a node with the example header color, teal
  #175C59. The focused text field has an outline in its lighter shade, #79D4C8 (spec 15.3).
  The header color shows nowhere else, except in the comparison row.
- No green, yellow or red in widget chrome. Those colors mean node state.
- Colors that are data are fine: color stops, the color picker, image pixels, the waveform.
- Same font, corner radius and spacing as the reference and the guide.

## Exact text

Required:

- Sheet title: **Patina node GUI widgets**
- Column titles: **Basic**, **Values**, **Canvas**
- Viewport title and caption: **Viewport**, "Large and full size only"
- Strip titles: **Compact and large**, **Fill color comparison**
- Comparison captions: **Neutral (default)**, **Header color (comparison)**

Illustrative: the widget captions, values, option names and table contents.

## Acceptance

- The 13 widgets of the Basic and Values groups are visible, plus the canvas, its four custom
  controls and the viewport.
- The slider, dropdown and curve show side by side at the compact and the large size.
- The comparison row shows the neutral and the header color version of the slider, toggle and
  button.
- No green, yellow or red in widget chrome.
- All text is sharp and readable at 100% zoom.
